Hello
everyone,

This time I have two pretty
simple questions regarding the proper implementation of left truncation in
camera trap distance sampling (CTDS).

We have a dataset of semi-automatically
generated observation distances with a minimum value of 1 m, therefore I
decided to remove all the distance estimates that are exactly 1 m and only use
the values of 1.1 m and more to fit the detection function on the unbinned data.

Now I am not sure about the
following points:

1. I would normally use the
right truncation distance as the ω parameter in the CTDS formula. Does this
still hold true when left-truncation is used in addition or would you subtract
the left truncation distance from the right truncation distance to obtain ω?

2. Animals beyond the
right-truncation distance are not counted, but what about animal observations with
distances that are equal to or smaller than the left-truncation distance (in
our case all animals with an observation distance of exactly 1 m)? Are they
also not considered for the nk parameter of the CTDS formula?

 Thanks and all the best,

 Maik

